# Steward session (cleanup after Bob / vibe ship)

Use when the user asks to clean up, harden, or remediate after a large Cursor/Bob commit, or when time-boxed (e.g. ~3h).

## Priority order (do not reorder)

1. **Dual SSOT / domain correctness** — delete legacy process clients; fix windows, projections, signup UX parity
2. **Contract sync** — types, API modules, e2e fixtures/mocks
3. **Broken imports / forms** — config forms must remain resolvable
4. **Tests** — projection/window/menu unit tests; e2e CTA/panel assertions
5. **Encode lessons** — Cursor rules / ADR notes
6. **God-file splits** — tables, report menu defs, shared form sections — only if ceilings fail or blocking the above

## Explicitly out of scope for a steward session

- Unrelated EventRoundWorkspace refactors
- Design-system rewrites
- New product features

## End of session

Leave the tree with: correctness fixed, tests/mocks green for touched paths, and at least one rule/checklist update so the next Cursor run sees the lesson.
